<section data-analytics-location="hero" class="subhero wrap" aria-labelledby="page-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / PRIVATE KUBERNETES IMPLEMENTATION</p><h1 id="page-title">A working platform.<br /><em>Knowledge to run it.</em></h1><p class="subhero-lede">When private Kubernetes is the right answer, we turn a defined workload and operating model into client-owned infrastructure. The finish line includes validation, documentation, and practical handoff.</p><div class="action-row"><a class="button" href="{{ landing.bookingUrl }}" data-booking>Discuss an implementation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="{{ 'Implementation question' | contactHref(page.url) }}">Email an implementation question <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><aside class="subhero-note"><span class="eyebrow">BUILT FOR OWNERSHIP</span><strong>Designed.<br />Validated.<br />Handed over.</strong><span aria-hidden="true">✳</span></aside></section>

<section data-analytics-location="process" class="section journey-section" aria-labelledby="build-flow-title"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">HOW A BUILD TAKES SHAPE</p><h2 id="build-flow-title">Define it. Build it.<br /><em>Prove it works.</em></h2></div><p class="heading-aside">Teams ready to build can come directly to this path. The assessment and proposal establish the scope before implementation begins.</p></div><ol class="process-list"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Understand the workload</h3><p>Review requirements, hardware, network, recovery needs, team capacity, and the fit for private infrastructure.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Agree on a fixed scope</h3><p>Document architecture, customer inputs, delivery milestones, acceptance criteria, exclusions, and responsibilities in a proposal.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Implement and validate</h3><p>Build the agreed platform and test the delivery, access, observability, and applicable recovery paths against the accepted scope.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h3>Hand over ownership</h3><p>Provide architecture and operating documentation, review the evidence, and work through practical sessions with the qualified operator.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>

<section data-analytics-location="scope" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="build-scope-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PLATFORM, AS A SYSTEM</p><h2 id="build-scope-title">The pieces work<br /><em>together.</em></h2></div><p class="heading-aside">Every project is scoped around the agreed workload and what the customer can operate afterward.</p></div><div class="offer-grid"><article><span class="eyebrow">FOUNDATION</span><h3 data-interest="platform_foundation">Private platform</h3><p>Client-owned compute, Kubernetes lifecycle, networking, storage, secure access, and deployment automation as required by the scope.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">READINESS</span><h3 data-interest="recovery">Operate and recover</h3><p>Monitoring, backups, recovery procedures, validation evidence, and an operating model suited to the workload.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">OWNERSHIP</span><h3 data-interest="handoff">Docs and handoff</h3><p>Architecture, inventory, runbooks, known risks, and guided sessions so the receiving team understands the result.</p></article></div><a class="text-link section-link" href="/deliverables/">Preview an illustrative handoff package <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>

<section data-analytics-location="fit" class="section split-callout" aria-labelledby="build-scope-boundary"><div class="wrap split-callout-inner"><div><p class="eyebrow">SCOPE SHAPES PRICE</p><h2 id="build-scope-boundary">A proposal tied<br /><em>to the actual work.</em></h2></div><div><p>Project fees follow workload and integration complexity, resilience and recovery requirements, hardware readiness, customer participation, and the agreed finish line. Discovery establishes fit; assessment and a written fixed-scope proposal define price and acceptance. Hardware, licenses, and on-site travel are customer costs unless specifically included.</p><p>The client owns hardware, accounts, configuration, and documentation. A qualified operator or IT provider owns routine operations and incident response after handoff. Scheduled advisory or platform care can be scoped separately; 24/7 on-call support is not offered.</p></div></div></section>

<section data-analytics-location="specialties" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="specialty-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHEN THE WORK CALLS FOR MORE</p><h2 id="specialty-title">Specialist additions.<br /><em>Only when they fit.</em></h2></div></div><div class="specialty-row"><p data-interest="gpu_ai">GPU and private AI enablement</p><p data-interest="vm_migration">Legacy-VM compatibility and phased migration</p><p data-interest="automation">Custom platform automation and integrations</p></div><p class="micro specialty-note">These are separately assessed and scoped, not default parts of a platform build.</p><p class="micro specialty-note">Still deciding what to build? <a href="/planning/">Explore cloud-native planning and team workshops.</a></p></section>

